--- body ---
## Decision (author, 2026-06-11)

**Option 1 — convert the manuscript to LaTeX**, tectonic-built like report and
slides, eliminating pandoc + pandoc-crossref entirely. Rationale: the Markdown
workflow accumulated complications (pandoc/pandoc-crossref version pinning,
CI/local divergence, raw-LaTeX escape blocks, the τ-glyph workaround) that
outweigh its benefits. Option 2 (local-only pandoc) is rejected.

Sequencing note: convert **before** the 0508 editorial rewrite, so the 0508
sub-tickets edit the LaTeX source once instead of editing `main.md` and
re-converting.

## Context
The manuscript build (`slides/manuscript/main.md` → `main.pdf`) depends on
`pandoc` + `pandoc-crossref` (introduced by ticket 0518 for symbolic
cross-references). The CI workflow `.github/workflows/docs-build.yml` was never
updated to install `pandoc-crossref`, so its "Build manuscript" step fails with
`Could not find executable pandoc-crossref` the moment it actually runs. PR #939
(a one-line Makefile comment change) was the first PR to trigger it and went red.

Compounding facts found 2026-06-10:
- CI's pandoc is **3.1.3** (apt on ubuntu-24.04); the author's local pandoc is a
  static **3.7.0.2** binary. So the two environments already diverge, and a
  matching `pandoc-crossref` differs by version (v0.3.20 needs pandoc ≥ 3.7.0.2;
  a 3.1.x-matching crossref would be older).
- The manuscript has effectively **never built in CI** — the `chore` path-filter
  also skipped it on every prior manuscript PR (see ticket 0525). #939 only
  triggered it because its diff was Makefile-only.
- `report.pdf` and `slides.pdf` are **tectonic-only** — they do not need pandoc
  at all. Only the manuscript pulls in the pandoc toolchain.

## Design direction (author, 2026-06-10)
"Use LaTeX instead of pandoc, and as few CI builds as possible." Minimise the CI
build matrix; do not pin a second pandoc + pandoc-crossref toolchain into CI just
to mirror the local manuscript build.

## Conversion plan (reverses ticket 0518's pandoc-crossref machinery)
1. Convert `slides/manuscript/main.md` → `slides/manuscript/main.tex`
   (one-shot `pandoc -t latex` as a starting point is fine; the committed
   result is hand-curated LaTeX, source of truth thereafter; delete `main.md`).
   - `{#sec:id}` / `[@sec:id]` / `[@fig:id]` / `{#tbl:id}` →
     `\label{...}` / `\Cref{...}` (cleveref) or `\ref`.
   - The `[-@sec:annex-…]` prefix-suppressed annex refs → `\appendix` +
     standard `\Cref` lettering; the raw-LaTeX escape blocks
     (`\renewcommand{\thefigure}{S\arabic{figure}}`,
     `\refstepcounter{figure}\label{…}`, `\includepdf` matrix) become plain
     LaTeX — no escaping needed.
   - The 0523 τ-glyph math-mode fix becomes moot (native LaTeX throughout).
2. `slides/Makefile`: `manuscript/main.pdf` rule becomes a tectonic build;
   drop the `PANDOC_CROSSREF` variable and the install comment (folded task
   below resolves by deletion).
3. `.github/workflows/docs-build.yml`: remove "Install pandoc" and rework
   "Build manuscript" to tectonic (or fold into the existing tectonic build
   steps) — as few CI builds as possible per the design direction.
4. `.claude/rules/writing.md`: replace the `main.md` pandoc-crossref house
   conventions with the LaTeX equivalents (`\label`/`\Cref`, unnumbered
   sections via `\section*`, annex conventions).
5. `tests/test_manuscript_crossref.py`: rewrite for LaTeX — no hand-typed
   "§N"/"Figure N"/"Annex X" literals in `main.tex` prose; every `\ref`/`\Cref`
   target has a matching `\label`. Keep
   `tests/test_manuscript_figure_numbering.py` and other manuscript adherence
   tests working against the `.tex` source.
6. Sweep for other `main.md` references (Makefile targets, docs, skills,
   tickets 0501/0507/0508 bodies note the path) — update paths in build
   plumbing; open tickets may keep stale paths, but in-flight ones (0501,
   0507, 0508) should be pointed at `main.tex` when they execute.

## Folded task
The `slides/Makefile` pandoc-crossref install comment (lines ~74–77, "compiled
against pandoc 3.1.x") is deleted along with the pandoc rule — resolves the
comment drift that closed PR #939 tried to fix prematurely.

## Relevant files
- `slides/manuscript/main.md` — the manuscript source (→ `main.tex`)
- `slides/Makefile` — `manuscript/main.pdf` rule + install comment
- `.github/workflows/docs-build.yml` — manuscript + pandoc install steps
- `.claude/rules/writing.md` — pandoc-crossref house conventions to replace
- `tests/test_manuscript_crossref.py` — adherence test to rewrite for LaTeX

## Exit criteria
- [x] Approach chosen and recorded: LaTeX conversion (author, 2026-06-11).
- [ ] `main.tex` builds locally via tectonic, content-equivalent to the last
      `main.md` build (same sections, figures, all cross-refs resolve).
- [ ] `main.md` deleted; no pandoc/pandoc-crossref references remain in
      Makefiles or CI.
- [ ] CI no longer fails on the manuscript / `pandoc-crossref`; report +
      slides CI still green.
- [ ] `.claude/rules/writing.md` conventions updated to LaTeX.
- [ ] Adherence tests (`test_manuscript_crossref.py`, figure numbering)
      rewritten for `.tex` and passing; `make check` passes.
